<%# Shared right-side navbar user section.
    Locals (all optional):
      balance_html     — raw HTML for balance display (e.g. Turf Monster wallet balance)
      extra_icons_html — raw HTML for app-specific icon buttons (e.g. refresh button)
      div2_html        — raw HTML to replace default Div 2 (e.g. Turf Monster seeds bar)

    WHY THIS FORK OF studio-engine's components/_user_nav STAYS (measured
    against 0.113.0, /tasks/turf-readopts-engine-navbar). The engine's copy
    takes balance_slot and div2_slot, and the avatar badge rides
    Studio.navbar_avatar_badge here too, but it would change the bar:
      1. the name and avatar are a link to account_path (or open the engine's
         link sidebar), never this app's gear sidebar ($store.sidebars.gearOpen);
      2. below md the name is screen-reader text, where this one shows it with
         the navUsernameFade mask;
      3. its icon rail draws the admin dropdown, not the gear sidebar trigger;
      4. it carries [data-nav-tools] and [data-nav-account], which engine.css
         restyles, not data-turf-nav-column and data-turf-nav-avatar, which
         this app's scroll-timeline rules scale;
      5. the freeEntryHover scope that joins the ✨ badge to the balance slot's
         peek lives on this wrapper; the engine seats the badge outside it.
    And the engine's layouts/_navbar cannot pass div2_slot to it at all. %>
<% balance_html     ||= nil %>
<% extra_icons_html ||= nil %>
<% div2_html        ||= nil %>
<% gear_toggle_action = "$store.sidebars.gearOpen = !$store.sidebars.gearOpen" %>
<% gear_expanded_attr = "$store.sidebars && $store.sidebars.gearOpen ? 'true' : 'false'" %>
<% gear_toggle_label = current_user&.admin? ? "Toggle admin menu" : "Toggle settings menu" %>

<%# freeEntryHover is the ✨ badge → balance-slot hover channel: the badge
    (rendered beside the avatar, Div 3) flips it and the balance slot inside
    balance_html reads it to peek "✨ Free Entry" over the amount. Alpine scope
    is DOM-based, so both live under this one wrapper. %>
<div class="flex gap-2 min-w-0" x-data="{ freeEntryHover: false }">
  <% if logged_in? %>
    <%# Left column: Div 1 + Div 2 stacked. data-turf-nav-column is the hook
        the scroll-timeline collapse scales (application.css, THE ACCOUNT ROW,
        SIZED AND ALIGNED AS ON THE HUB): balance, icons, name and level shrink
        together by 7/8 from the right edge, by the same transform, and slide
        right by the 8px the avatar gives up, so the block stays one piece at
        both sizes and the name keeps its gap to the avatar. self-center, not
        the row's default stretch: the 40px avatar is taller than the two rows,
        and stretched they would sit at the top of its box and report its
        height, which hides the 2px hydrate nav_band_watch.js listens for. %>
    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 self-center" data-turf-nav-column>
      <%# Div 1 (Bigger): balance + icons + username — margin-left matches Div 2's seeds bar offset so cash aligns with bar start.
          pr-1.5 on a phone; from 768px none, so the name ends on the
          column's edge and its gap to the avatar is the hub's 12px (see Div 3). %>
      <div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 leading-none pr-1.5 md:pr-0" style="margin-left: -6px;">
        <% if balance_html.present? %>
          <%= raw balance_html %>
        <% end %>
        <%# The theme toggle leads the gear, a size down at 14px, as on every
            engine navbar (studio-engine's components/_user_nav). The gear is
            already the 16px glyph the engine sizes its own to. %>
        <span class="hidden md:flex flex-shrink-0 items-center gap-2 ml-auto">
          <span class="flex scale-[0.875]" data-nav-theme-toggle="desktop"><%= render "components/theme_toggle_morph" %></span>
          <span class="hidden md:block"><%= render "components/gear_sidebar_trigger" %></span>
        </span>
        <%# nav-username sizes off --nav-p (lg -> base) — see the navbar's
            nav-shell comment. transition-colors, not transition-all: the old
            transition-all also put this button's font-size on a 300ms clock
            that kept running after the finger stopped. %>
        <button type="button"
                class="nav-username dm-coral min-w-0 max-w-[4.5rem] min-[400px]:max-w-[6rem] md:max-w-[7rem] text-heading font-semibold hover:text-primary transition-colors duration-300 leading-none md:ml-0 ml-auto overflow-hidden whitespace-nowrap text-left bg-transparent border-0 p-0"
                @click.stop="<%= gear_toggle_action %>"
                aria-label="<%= gear_toggle_label %>"
                aria-controls="gear-sidebar gear-sidebar-mobile"
                aria-haspopup="dialog"
                :aria-expanded="<%= gear_expanded_attr %>"
                data-username-display="true"
                <%# navUsernameFade (shared/_alpine_factories) re-measures on every
                    box change via ResizeObserver. It used to be an inline one-shot
                    here and the mask never followed the balance hydrate, the Free
                    Entry face swap, or a resize across the squeeze band. %>
                x-data="navUsernameFade()"
                x-bind:style="overflows ? '-webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black 50%, transparent); mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black 50%, transparent);' : ''">
          <%= current_user.display_name %>
        </button>
      </div>
      <%# Div 2 (Smaller): 5-section seeds bar + level (right) — see components/_seeds_bar %>
      <% solana_label = current_user.respond_to?(:truncated_solana) && current_user.try(:solana_connected?) ? current_user.truncated_solana : nil %>
      <div class="mt-0.5 min-w-[8rem]" style="margin-left: -6px;">
        <%= render "components/seeds_bar",
              seeds_data: display_seeds_data,
              compact: true,
              label: solana_label,
              shimmer_interval: 9 %>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%# Div 3 (Avatar): spans both rows — the ✨ free-entry badge SITS ON the
        avatar's upper-left corner, the way a notification dot rides a profile
        picture.
        Absolutely positioned on purpose: the badge then costs the row NO width
        whether or not the user holds a token. A flow-based tuck (negative
        margin) can't do that — the badge's `.hidden` lives on the BUTTON so
        updateNavTokens can surface it without a reload, and the wrapper it
        leaves behind would still eat the negative margin and drag the avatar
        left into the username.
        z-20 > the avatar's z-10 puts the badge ON TOP. It opens a stacking
        context, which is fine at 20: nothing inside the badge has to escape it
        now that the count popover is gone (the badge opens the gear sidebar,
        which renders at the layout root), and the whole context still outranks
        the avatar. z-0 here would invert that and bury the badge.
        ml-3 reserves the 8px of badge that overhangs the avatar — the badge is
        out of flow, so without it the username (which grows to fill Div 1) runs
        right up under the sparkle. From 768px it is md:ml-1: with the row's
        gap-2 that is 12px from the column's edge, where the name ends (Div 1
        drops its padding there), the hub's name-to-avatar gap (the engine's
        --nav-gap, 0.75rem). The badge still clears the name by 4px. %>
    <%# data-turf-nav-avatar: the avatar is 40px at rest and 32px collapsed
        from 768px, as on the hub (application.css). The badge rides inside,
        so it scales with the avatar it sits on. %>
    <div class="relative ml-3 md:ml-1 flex flex-shrink-0 items-center" data-turf-nav-avatar>
      <%# Studio.navbar_avatar_badge (studio-engine 0.113.0) names the badge;
          this wrapper seats it. The engine's [data-nav-avatar-badge] seat is
          sized for its own account row (a 2rem box on the row's right edge),
          not this 40px avatar, so the fork keeps its own -left-2 -top-1 seat
          and does not carry that hook. %>
      <% avatar_badge = studio_navbar_avatar_badge %>
      <% if avatar_badge %><div class="absolute -left-2 -top-1 z-20"><%= studio_navbar_slot_tag(avatar_badge) %></div><% end %>
      <button type="button"
              class="dm-green relative z-10 hover:opacity-80 transition flex-shrink-0 flex items-center bg-transparent border-0 p-0"
              @click.stop="<%= gear_toggle_action %>"
              aria-label="<%= gear_toggle_label %>"
              aria-controls="gear-sidebar gear-sidebar-mobile"
              aria-haspopup="dialog"
              :aria-expanded="<%= gear_expanded_attr %>"
              data-profile-image-toggle="true">
        <%= render "components/avatar", user: current_user, size: "nav" %>
      </button>
    </div>
  <% else %>
    <span class="hidden md:flex scale-[0.875]"><%= render "components/theme_toggle" %></span>
    <span class="hidden md:block"><%= render "components/gear_sidebar_trigger" %></span>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 ml-auto">
      <%# Opens the in-page auth modal (credentials step: Google + wallet + email
          magic-link). href=/signin is the no-JS fallback — the page still exists,
          we just don't route to it from here for now. %>
      <%= link_to "Sign in", signin_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-sm",
            "@click.prevent": "$store.modals.open('auth', { step: 'credentials', mode: 'signup', submitting: null, formError: '', phantomError: '', googleError: '' })" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
